scope: Cline Pass's API is OpenAI-compatible ONLY when streaming. NON-streaming responses come back wrapped as `{"data":{…},"success":true}` with NO top-level `choices`; Charon relays the body verbatim, so a non-streaming OpenAI client hitting a cline-pass-backed pool gets an unparseable body. Add a PROVIDER-SCOPED (cline-pass only) response-unwrap shim on the non-streaming relay path: when the served upstream provider is `cline-pass` and the response is non-streaming, unwrap `{"data":…}` → the inner OpenAI object before relaying (leave streaming/SSE untouched — it's already clean). Also handle opencode's auxiliary title/summary `generateText` if it's non-streaming.
